# Use the project venv

This repo has `.venv` at the project root (Python 3.12+). **Always** use it for Python, pip, pytest, ruff, uvicorn, and other Python CLIs. Never use the first `python`/`pip` on PATH — on Windows that is often Store Python 3.10 and will install into the wrong environment.

```powershell
# ✅ GOOD
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e ".[dev]"
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m ruff check --fix .
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload

# ❌ BAD
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python -m pytest
py -m pip install ...
```

If `.venv` is missing, create it with Python 3.12+ (`py -3.13 -m venv .venv` or `uv venv --python 3.13`) and install with `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e ".[dev]"`.
